{:edb/db-before-t 1163 :edb/db-after-t 1164 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534476 50 #inst "2026-10-07T07:23:55.400Z" 13194139534476 true] [17592186100642 1100 "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $y' = 5y$ that satisfies $y(0)=3$." 13194139534476 false] [17592186100642 1100 "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $y' = 5y$ that satisfies $y(0)=3.$" 13194139534476 true] [17592186100642 1145 "We first find the general solution, and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= 5y \\\\\n\\frac{1}{y}\\frac{dy}{dx} &= 5 \\\\\n\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{dy}{dx}dx &= 5\\int dx \\\\\n\\int \\frac{1}{y}dy &= 5\\int dx \\\\\n\\ln \\mid y \\mid &= 5x + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the exponential function to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &= \\pm  e^{5x + C} \\\\\n&= \\pm  e^{C}e^{5x} \\\\\n&= Ke^{5x}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm e^{C}$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nNow we apply the condition $y(0) = 3$ to find $K$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny(0) &= 3 \\\\\nKe^{5 \\cdot 0} &= 3 \\\\\nK &= 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $y' = 5y$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=3$ is\n\n$$\ny = 3 e^{5x} \\,\n$$" 13194139534476 false] [17592186100642 1145 "We first find the general solution, and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =5y \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =5 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =5\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =5\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =5x+C\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the exponential function to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm {e}^{5x+C} \\\\  & =\\pm {e}^{C}{e}^{5x} \\\\  & =K{e}^{5x}\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm e^{C}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nNow we apply the condition $y(0) = 3$ to find $K\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =3 \\\\ K{e}^{5\\cdot 0} & =3 \\\\ K & =3\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $y' = 5y$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=3$ is\n\n$$\ny = 3 e^{5x}  \\,.\n$$" 13194139534476 true] [17592186100646 1100 "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\cos(3y)\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y} {\\textrm{d}x} + \\sin(2x) = 0$ given that  $y\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\\right) = 0.$ Assume that $-\\dfrac{\\pi}{6} < y < \\dfrac{\\pi}{6} .$" 13194139534476 true] [17592186100646 1100 "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\cos(3y)\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y} {\\textrm{d}x} + \\sin(2x) = 0$ given that $y\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\\right) = 0$. Assume that $-\\dfrac{\\pi}{6} < y < \\dfrac{\\pi}{6}$." 13194139534476 false] [17592186100646 1145 "We first find the general solution, and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos (3y)\\frac{dy}{dx} &= -\\sin (2x) \\\\\n\\int \\cos (3y)\\frac{dy}{dx}dx &= - \\int \\sin (2x)dx \\\\\n\\int \\cos (3y)dy &= - \\int \\sin (2x)dx \\\\\n\\frac{1}{3}\\sin (3y) &= \\frac{1}{2}\\cos (2x) + C \\\\\n\\sin (3y) &= \\frac{3}{2}\\cos (2x) + C_{1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C_1=3C$.\n\nNow let's apply the condition\n\n$$\ny\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\\right) = 0\n$$\n\nto find $C_1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) &= 0 \\\\\n\\sin (3 \\cdot 0) &= \\frac{3}{2}\\cos (2 \\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4}) + C_{1} \\\\\n\\sin (0) &= \\frac{3}{2}\\cos (\\frac{\\pi }{2}) + C_{1} \\\\\n0 &= 0 + C_{1} \\\\\nC_{1} &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we get the particular solution in implicit form:\n\n$$\n\\sin(3y) = \\dfrac {3} {2} \\cos(2x)\n$$" 13194139534476 false] [17592186100646 1145 "We first find the general solution, and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x) \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\,\\text{d}y & =-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3y) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+C \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3y) & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+{C}_{1}\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C_1=3C.$\n\nNow let's apply the condition $y\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\\right) = 0$ to find $C_1\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot 0) & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})+{C}_{1} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(0) & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+{C}_{1} \\\\ 0 & =0+{C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{1} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we get the particular solution in implicit form:\n\n$$\n\\sin(3y)   =  \\dfrac {3} {2} \\cos(2x)\n$$" 13194139534476 true] [17592186100806 1020 #edb/ref 17592186290333 13194139534476 true] [17592186100806 1020 #edb/ref 17592186290354 13194139534476 true] [17592186100806 1020 #edb/ref 17592186290367 13194139534476 true] [17592186100806 1020 #edb/ref 17592186290374 13194139534476 true] [17592186100807 1020 #edb/ref 17592186290340 13194139534476 true] [17592186100807 1020 #edb/ref 17592186290347 13194139534476 true] [17592186100807 1020 #edb/ref 17592186290357 13194139534476 true] [17592186100807 1020 #edb/ref 17592186290360 13194139534476 true] [17592186100807 1020 #edb/ref 17592186290364 13194139534476 true] [17592186101309 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534476 true] [17592186101309 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534476 false] [17592186101309 1100 "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2x}{{y}^{2}}$ that satisfies $y(2)=\\sqrt[3]{13}.$" 13194139534476 true] [17592186101309 1100 "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{2x}{y^{2}}$ that satisfies $y(2) = \\sqrt[3]{13}$." 13194139534476 false] [17592186101309 1145 "Separate and integrate:\n$$y^2\\,dy=2x\\,dx,\\qquad \\frac{y^3}{3}=x^2+C.$$\nWrite $y^3=3x^2+K$ and apply $y(2)=\\sqrt[3]{13}$:\n$$13=12+K,\\qquad K=1.$$\nTherefore $y^3=3x^2+1$, or $y=\\sqrt[3]{3x^2+1}$." 13194139534476 false] [17592186101309 1145 "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2x}{{y}^{2}} \\\\ {y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x \\\\ \\int {y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{3}}{3} & ={x}^{2}+{C}_{1} \\\\ {y}^{3} & =3{x}^{2}+3{C}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the general solution is\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}=3{x}^{2}+C,\n$$\n\nwhere $C=3{C}_{1}$  is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(2)=\\sqrt[3]{13}$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\sqrt[3]{13})}^{3} & =3(2)^{2}+C \\\\ 13 & =12+C \\\\ C & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2x}{{y}^{2}}$ that satisfies the condition $y(2)=\\sqrt[3]{13}$ is\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}=3{x}^{2}+1.\n$$" 13194139534476 true] [17592186290333 1017 #edb/ref 17592186290334 13194139534476 true] [17592186290333 1089 "q-104055" 13194139534476 true] [17592186290333 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534476 true] [17592186290333 1100 "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y}$ that satisfies $y(0)=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" 13194139534476 true] [17592186290333 1113 #uuid "a2470563-1a2f-5e0a-b7d9-e6883d815fd3" 13194139534476 true] [17592186290333 1145 "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡y & =x+C \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡y & =-x-C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =-0-C \\\\ 0 & =0-C \\\\ C & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we get the particular solution in implicit form:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡y=-x\n$$" 13194139534476 true] [17592186290334 1000 #edb/ref 17592186290335 13194139534476 true] [17592186290334 1000 #edb/ref 17592186290336 13194139534476 true] [17592186290334 1000 #edb/ref 17592186290337 13194139534476 true] [17592186290334 1000 #edb/ref 17592186290338 13194139534476 true] [17592186290334 1000 #edb/ref 17592186290339 13194139534476 true] [17592186290334 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534476 true] [17592186290334 1041 "selection" 13194139534476 true] [17592186290334 1104 #edb/ref 17592186290336 13194139534476 true] [17592186290334 1110 #uuid "cb92c282-cf61-5b85-93a2-fb47c1fb258d" 13194139534476 true] [17592186290335 1034 "\\operatorname{cos}⁡y=x+1" 13194139534476 true] [17592186290335 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534476 true] [17592186290335 1111 #uuid "4dc3f3e0-ff57-5efd-bd2a-2ae7c331785c" 13194139534476 true] [17592186290336 1034 "\\operatorname{cos}⁡y=-x" 13194139534476 true] [17592186290336 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534476 true] [17592186290336 1111 #uuid "13cc58bb-55ce-5b90-bc27-e0d82b697e61" 13194139534476 true] [17592186290337 1034 "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y=x" 13194139534476 true] [17592186290337 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534476 true] [17592186290337 1111 #uuid "c22f6665-5738-56da-b581-b8d90a921abf" 13194139534476 true] [17592186290338 1034 "\\operatorname{cos}⁡2y=-2x+1" 13194139534476 true] [17592186290338 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534476 true] [17592186290338 1111 #uuid "4cf097b4-cf1f-5a26-939d-f3154132a89b" 13194139534476 true] [17592186290339 1034 "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y=-2x" 13194139534476 true] [17592186290339 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534476 true] [17592186290339 1111 #uuid "1f1214e9-480e-5e00-9d58-fabbe34483df" 13194139534476 true] [17592186290340 1017 #edb/ref 17592186290341 13194139534476 true] [17592186290340 1089 "q-104064" 13194139534476 true] [17592186290340 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534476 true] [17592186290340 1100 "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=3{y}^{2}{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}{x}^{3}$ that satisfies $y(2)=\\frac{1}{8}.$" 13194139534476 true] [17592186290340 1113 #uuid "76f508a1-f65b-5d1d-8bbf-94be0b492cbb" 13194139534476 true] [17592186290340 1145 "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{y}^{2}{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}{x}^{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={y}^{2}(3{x}^{2}-4{x}^{3}) \\\\ \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2}-4{x}^{3} \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (3{x}^{2}-4{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =3\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-4\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{y} & ={x}^{3}-{x}^{4}+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}-{x}^{3}-C}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(2)=\\frac{1}{8}$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(2) & =\\frac{1}{8} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{2}^{4}-{2}^{3}-C} & =\\frac{1}{8} \\\\ \\frac{1}{8-C} & =\\frac{1}{8} \\\\ C & =0\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=3{y}^{2}{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}{x}^{3}$ that satisfies the condition $y(2)=\\frac{1}{8}$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}-{x}^{3}}\\,.\n$$" 13194139534476 true] [17592186290341 1000 #edb/ref 17592186290342 13194139534476 true] [17592186290341 1000 #edb/ref 17592186290343 13194139534476 true] [17592186290341 1000 #edb/ref 17592186290344 13194139534476 true] [17592186290341 1000 #edb/ref 17592186290345 13194139534476 true] [17592186290341 1000 #edb/ref 17592186290346 13194139534476 true] [17592186290341 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534476 true] [17592186290341 1041 "selection" 13194139534476 true] [17592186290341 1104 #edb/ref 17592186290342 13194139534476 true] [17592186290341 1110 #uuid "062b6761-8a83-56a7-ab24-c797cc9067ea" 13194139534476 true] [17592186290342 1034 "y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}-{x}^{3}}" 13194139534476 true] [17592186290342 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534476 true] [17592186290342 1111 #uuid "4bc12d2e-e51b-5a42-96cd-b305f65fb37f" 13194139534476 true] [17592186290343 1034 "y=\\frac{1}{2{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}}" 13194139534476 true] [17592186290343 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534476 true] [17592186290343 1111 #uuid "db1c7f3a-6ecc-55c5-809a-0863430e9877" 13194139534476 true] [17592186290344 1034 "y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-16}" 13194139534476 true] [17592186290344 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534476 true] [17592186290344 1111 #uuid "98c45658-526f-5c3d-a7a4-904eaec5c7b0" 13194139534476 true] [17592186290345 1034 "y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}-{x}^{4}+16}" 13194139534476 true] [17592186290345 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534476 true] [17592186290345 1111 #uuid "eb56b96c-6b1e-5509-9c5c-9